{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1449523-species-speed-factor","id":1449523,"title":"Species speed factor?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-25T02:12:59-07:00","id":1449523,"title":"Species speed factor?","content":"URSHUL<br /> Traits: Strength +2, Dexterity +2, Stamina +2, Manipulation<br /> \u20131, Size +1, Species speed factor +3 (Health +3,<br /> Initiative +2, Speed +7).<br /> <br /> URHAN<br /> Traits: Dexterity +2, Stamina +1, Manipulation \u20131, Size<br /> \u20131, Species speed factor +3 (Initiative +2, Speed +5).<br /> <br /> What does the &quot;Species speed factor +3&quot; indicates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1005-lukezs","name":"LukeZS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T03:58:23-07:00","id":1449528,"title":"","content":"It's described in the Traits section of Chapter Four (I think).<br /> <br /> Every creature has a Species factor for calculating Speed. Human adults have 5, wolves have 8. Werewolves in wolf forms use a wolf's species factor for calculating Speed. The +3 indicates the change made to the trait from the baseline i.e. human template (5 + 3 = 8)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T04:17:38-07:00","id":1449534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1449523-species-speed-factor?p=1449528#post1449528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's described in the Traits section of Chapter Four (I think).<br /> <br /> Every creature has a Species factor for calculating Speed. Human adults have 5, wolves have 8. Werewolves in wolf forms use a wolf's species factor for calculating Speed. The +3 indicates the change made to the trait from the baseline i.e. human template (5 + 3 = 8)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So why for the wolf-form it also specify &quot;Speed +5&quot;? It's +3 or +5 ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1005,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1005-lukezs","user":"LukeZS","date":". 05-25-2021, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1005-lukezs","name":"LukeZS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T04:24:39-07:00","id":1449535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LukeZS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1449523-species-speed-factor?p=1449534#post1449534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So why for the wolf-form it also specify &quot;Speed +5&quot;? It's +3 or +5 ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speed = Strength + Dexterity + Species factor<br /> <br /> So for Urhan, it's +5 (Speed) = +0 (Strength) +2 (Dexterity) +3 (Species factor)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T04:40:30-07:00","id":1449538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1449523-species-speed-factor?p=1449535#post1449535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speed = Strength + Dexterity + Species factor<br /> <br /> So for Urhan, it's +5 (Speed) = +0 (Strength) +2 (Dexterity) +3 (Species factor)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah ok, it's the total already calculated. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1005-lukezs","name":"LukeZS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1005_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}